1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,300
using language, reading and writing.

2
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:11,160
Copernicus' Revolutionary Theory

3
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:17,940
Nicolaus Copernicus was frightened and his mind was confused.

4
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:25,180
Although he had tried to ignore them, all his mathematical calculations led to the same conclusion

5
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:30,400
that the Earth was not the center of the solar system.

6
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:37,880
Only if you put the sun there did the movements of the other planets in the sky make sense.

7
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:45,660
Yet he could not tell anyone about his theory as the powerful Christian Church would have punished him

8
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:47,720
for even suggesting such an idea.

9
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:05,760
The problem arose because astronomers had noticed that some planets in the sky seemed to stop,

10
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,600
move backward and then go forward in a loop.

11
00:01:10,720 --> 00:01:14,780
Others appeared brighter at times and less bright at others.

12
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:29,520
Copernicus had thought long and hard about these problems and tried to find an answer.

13
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:37,280
He had collected observations of the stars and used all his mathematical knowledge to explain them.

14
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:41,420
But only his new theory could do that.

15
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:48,180
So between 1510 and 1514 he worked on it,

16
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:52,620
gradually improving his theory until he felt it was complete.

17
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:58,720
In 1514 he showed it privately to his friends.

18
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:02,760
The changes he made to the old theory were revolutionary.

19
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:18,200
He also suggested that the earth was spinning as it went round the sun

20
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:24,060
and this explained changes in the movement of the planets and in the brightness of the stars.

21
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:30,180
His friends were enthusiastic and encouraged him to publish his ideas,

22
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,300
but Copernicus was cautious.

23
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:37,580
He did not want to be attacked by the Christian Church,

24
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:42,720
so he only published it as he lay dying in 1543.

25
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:47,100
Certainly he was right to be careful.

26
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:50,080
The Christian Church rejected his theory,

27
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:56,540
saying it was against God's idea and people who supported it would be attacked.

28
00:02:57,240 --> 00:03:03,560
Yet Copernicus' theory is now the basis on which all our ideas of the universe are built.

29
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,920
Copernicus showed this was obviously wrong.

30
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:23,520
Now people can see that there is a direct link between his theory

31
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:28,600
and the work of Isaac Newton, Albert Einstein and Stephen Hawking.
